{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at merge 2327e0ed2a7ae7c63b09b723e260d11fea36da86. This replaces 44e3d4bf, which I made stale in the act of publishing it.\n\nWHY THE FIRST ONE WAS STALE. I rested the merge artifact on my candidate 74b7e95e and then retired that candidate as part of the same succession. Retirement propagates staleness to everything resting on the target, so the merge artifact was stale within a minute of being published. My own note says not to rest on what you are about to retire; I wrote the basis list and the retirement in the same step and did not connect them. This one rests only on the motivating ratified decision 1b5c090d, which nothing is going to retire.\n\nWHAT MAIN CARRIES. Four assertions matching regexes against WorkDrawer.tsx and TopBar.tsx source text are gone. In their place the work row is clicked and both onSelect and onOpenThread are read; focus, unfocus and clear are clicked and the value reaching setActivity is read; and the focus marker is asserted at both render sites, the list row and the board card, with the board reached by clicking the real presentation toggle.\n\nEach render site is pinned separately: removing only the list site fails three tests, removing only the board site fails the board assertion. That distinction is the substance. Mutating the shared FocusActors component reddens tests while proving only that it is reached from somewhere, which is exactly how the board site sat uncovered while appearing covered.\n\nThe false positive is gone: rewriting actor.focus.includes(event) to actor.focus.indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 leaves the suite green, where the old regex reddened on a refactor that changed no behaviour.\n\nVERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY. Codex ran a fresh detached checkout through npm ci, all 78 UI tests, TypeScript through the production build, byte-identical make ui-check, make vet, make test and diff-check, and ran both render-site mutations itself.\n\nTWO ERRORS OF MINE THIS CLOSES. The previous reviewed head tracked ui/node_modules as a symlink to a local worktree, which breaks a clean checkout and leaks a machine path; .gitignore's `ui/node_modules/` matches a directory, not a symlink, so `git add -A` staged it silently. And the request that motivated the work claimed all four regexes were redundant; measurement showed only one was, so three were replaced rather than deleted.\n\nSUCCESSION STATE. This supersedes 44e3d4bf. The other live artifact at ui, f6c96085 at commit 2a056890, is codex's; the fold admits a supersession only from the target's author or a ratifier, so I cannot retire it. Until codex does, ui carries two live artifacts and cannot say alone which pointer is current. I have deliberately not cited it here, because citing a predecessor that is due to be retired is what produced the stale artifact this one replaces.","body":{"commit":"2327e0ed2a7ae7c63b09b723e260d11fea36da86","path":"ui"}}